  "interpretation": "<table style=\"width: 81.4732%; height: 89.8px;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" data-cke-table-faked-selection-table=\"\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.4px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 12.0345%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;Result</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 87.9292%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;Remarks</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 42px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 12.0345%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;Positive</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 87.9292%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;Indicates presence of circulating Cryptococcus species complex Antigen</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25.4px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 12.0345%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;Negative</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 87.9292%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;Indicates absence of circulating Cryptococcus species complex Antigen</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\"><strong>Note:</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Positive results are seen in fungal disease of lungs, brain and meninges caused by Cryptococcus species complex (C. neoformans &amp; C. gattii). While the majority of C. neoformans infections occur in immunocompromised patients, C. gattii has a higher predilection for infection in healthy individuals.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Negative results are seen in absence of Cryptococcus infection. However, it does not rule out the disease.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Results should be co-related with clinical condition and tests like microscopy and fungal culture.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">False positive results may be observed in patients with high levels of Rheumatoid factor, conditions like trichosporonosis, Capnocytophaga canimorus septicaemia, malignancy, Rothia bacteremia, usage of some soaps, disinfectants and hydroxyethyl starch (used for fluid resuscitation).</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">False negative reaction may be due to processing of sample collected early in the course of disease or low threshold of antigen and due to prozone effect. The test should be repeated on a new specimen obtained after two weeks.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Test conducted in CSF/serum.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\"><strong>Uses</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">To diagnose disease caused by Cryptococcus species complex (C. neoformans).</span><br></li>\n</ul>",
